WEBVTT

00:01:41.390 --> 00:01:42.350
Who's there?

00:01:42.950 --> 00:01:47.520
What's so fun about stealing something so boring?

00:01:49.360 --> 00:01:52.330
It <i>is </i>fun, Lupin.

00:01:52.990 --> 00:01:56.340
I am decorated by treasure.

00:01:56.340 --> 00:02:00.180
The more I steal, the more special I become.

00:02:00.180 --> 00:02:03.100
I don't know whether
your greed is deep or shallow.

00:02:06.340 --> 00:02:08.980
So? Why are you here?

00:02:10.020 --> 00:02:12.300
Why am I here?

00:02:14.850 --> 00:02:17.550
My, this is rather straightforward.

00:02:17.550 --> 00:02:18.460
Huh?

00:02:18.960 --> 00:02:21.310
You don't dislike jewel roses, do you?

00:02:21.310 --> 00:02:23.350
They aren't bad.

00:02:23.350 --> 00:02:25.570
But red's such a common color.

00:02:25.570 --> 00:02:26.530
In that case...

00:02:26.530 --> 00:02:28.240
As you wish.

00:02:31.240 --> 00:02:33.430
Alexandrite, huh?

00:02:33.430 --> 00:02:36.010
A gem whose color depends on the
wavelength of light passing through it.

00:02:36.010 --> 00:02:39.510
Under daylight, it's blue and by firelight, it's red.

00:02:40.240 --> 00:02:42.350
Does it please you?

00:02:43.530 --> 00:02:45.280
This is worth what you saw while peeping on me.

00:02:45.930 --> 00:02:49.630
But if you want to seduce me with alexandrite,
you need to bring me the biggest one there is.

00:02:49.630 --> 00:02:53.600
You're telling me to steal the one in the Smithsonian?

00:02:53.600 --> 00:02:55.090
You're pretty full of yourself.

00:02:55.830 --> 00:02:59.470
If you raise the bar too high, you'll set yourself up for a hard fall.

00:02:59.470 --> 00:03:01.470
Thanks for your concern.

00:03:03.560 --> 00:03:06.150
Do you want me that badly?

00:03:06.150 --> 00:03:11.310
I make it a point to steal everything I send out my calling card for.

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:14.170
Then how about this?

00:03:14.170 --> 00:03:18.620
You know they found a new pyramid in Egypt, right?

00:03:18.620 --> 00:03:20.870
It was buried under the sand until now, right?

00:03:20.870 --> 00:03:23.140
Officially, yes.

00:03:23.140 --> 00:03:27.660
But it looks like some old looters had already found it.

00:03:27.660 --> 00:03:31.880
In any era, thieves always have the best intel.

00:03:32.750 --> 00:03:37.390
They say there's a smiling peacock with red wings in there.

00:03:37.390 --> 00:03:40.980
I've heard of it, but only rumors.

00:03:40.980 --> 00:03:46.650
There's a legend that says whoever holds that peacock will obtain great wealth.

00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:57.800
On one side of the scale is Maat's feather of truth.

00:03:58.120 --> 00:04:03.210
The dead person weighs their own heart against it.

00:04:03.890 --> 00:04:10.670
If the sins accrued during life are heavy enough to tip the scales, he will never be reborn.

00:04:10.670 --> 00:04:14.510
This is called the "Judgment of the Dead."

00:04:20.140 --> 00:04:21.730
Hey, get away from him!

00:04:22.890 --> 00:04:26.240
If you get near a scary man like him,
you'll get kidnapped.

00:04:27.480 --> 00:04:32.700
<i>Looks like I can't conceal my
sordid past, no matter where I go.</i>

00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:41.710
<i>I don't expect to be reborn into a proper life,</i>

00:04:42.760 --> 00:04:44.780
<i>but my future looks pretty uncertain.</i>

00:04:49.490 --> 00:04:50.420
Mister.

00:04:51.750 --> 00:04:53.140
Mister!

00:04:53.740 --> 00:04:56.460
Won't you come weigh your sins?

00:04:56.460 --> 00:04:57.660
I'll make it cheap for ya.

00:04:57.660 --> 00:05:00.610
Weigh my sins, huh?

00:05:00.610 --> 00:05:03.370
So it's like the "Judgment of the Dead."

00:05:03.370 --> 00:05:05.730
If you already know,
then I won't bother explaining it.

00:05:05.730 --> 00:05:08.380
See? They weigh the same.

00:05:08.380 --> 00:05:10.520
But when you hold this heart,

00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:14.030
remember your past sins and weigh it again...

00:05:15.300 --> 00:05:18.140
You sayin' the weight will change?

00:05:18.140 --> 00:05:20.170
There's just some trick to it, right?

00:05:20.170 --> 00:05:21.830
Are you scared, Mister?

00:05:21.830 --> 00:05:23.790
Have you done a lot of bad things?

00:05:23.790 --> 00:05:25.050
What?

00:05:25.050 --> 00:05:27.540
It's written all over your face.

00:05:33.930 --> 00:05:36.160
Hmph, ridiculous.

00:05:36.160 --> 00:05:37.410
Wait up.

00:05:38.450 --> 00:05:39.550
You with him?

00:05:44.470 --> 00:05:45.560
You...!

00:05:50.070 --> 00:05:52.360
Damn, even the monkey was in on it?

00:05:52.360 --> 00:05:55.110
This is the only thing that's still safe.

00:05:58.260 --> 00:06:01.570
This worn out thing? It's not worth anything.

00:06:01.570 --> 00:06:04.990
And can you even live without it?

00:06:04.990 --> 00:06:07.870
You don't seem like a man who
can earn a respectable living.

00:06:07.870 --> 00:06:09.830
Leave me be.

00:06:09.830 --> 00:06:10.890
How about it?

00:06:11.420 --> 00:06:17.520
If you really need money, I can tell you about an interesting job.

00:06:26.160 --> 00:06:29.520
So I have to steal this smiling peacock?

00:06:30.070 --> 00:06:32.720
There's no end of people who want it.

00:06:32.720 --> 00:06:37.650
Anyone connected to the underground in this country will know the legend.

00:06:37.650 --> 00:06:42.110
"The red-winged smiling peacock brings great wealth."

00:06:42.110 --> 00:06:44.160
I've heard stories like that before.

00:06:44.160 --> 00:06:48.100
It's a common theme of legends, isn't it?

00:06:48.100 --> 00:06:50.160
And there's many variations of it.

00:06:50.650 --> 00:06:53.870
"The blue-winged peacock brings death",

00:06:53.870 --> 00:06:55.170
for instance.

00:07:09.190 --> 00:07:12.350
This old well is the entrance.

00:07:12.350 --> 00:07:16.190
Few who venture inside ever return.

00:07:16.910 --> 00:07:20.900
They say the pyramids are brimming with curses.

00:07:27.960 --> 00:07:31.160
Were these guys after the red peacock too?

00:07:42.650 --> 00:07:45.250
Leave this place!

00:07:45.250 --> 00:07:47.760
Or you shall be punished!

00:07:49.380 --> 00:07:51.770
A mechanism ignites some gas,

00:07:51.770 --> 00:07:55.150
and the shadowy pharaoh is a drawing made with oil.

00:07:55.150 --> 00:07:57.150
The voice comes from a speaker.

00:08:00.370 --> 00:08:01.780
Someone's there!

00:08:13.070 --> 00:08:15.760
They even used his burial artifacts?

00:08:16.540 --> 00:08:23.300
This curse... is nothing more than the looters... trying to trip each other up!

00:08:27.970 --> 00:08:31.720
Leave! Or else...

00:08:33.680 --> 00:08:36.060
Did you hear me? Leave...

00:08:48.460 --> 00:08:50.040
Come on.

00:08:50.050 --> 00:08:53.140
I was even nice enough to warn you.

00:08:53.140 --> 00:08:56.180
Grave robbers like you will get punished.

00:08:56.180 --> 00:08:57.500
And what about yourself?

00:08:57.500 --> 00:09:00.670
I'm an unnamed thief.

00:09:00.670 --> 00:09:03.760
For those of us who specialize in
tough jobs, I'm a pro among pros.

00:09:03.760 --> 00:09:06.510
So what's with this cheap setup?

00:09:06.510 --> 00:09:09.250
And here I thought you'd enjoy it.

00:09:10.060 --> 00:09:13.010
What did you come here to steal?
Depending on your answer...

00:09:13.970 --> 00:09:16.400
What if I answered "peacock"?

00:09:16.400 --> 00:09:18.480
Worst possible answer.

00:09:23.310 --> 00:09:25.070
Looks like we'll have to go again.

00:09:27.990 --> 00:09:28.780
Three.

00:09:30.070 --> 00:09:30.780
Two.

00:09:32.030 --> 00:09:32.680
One.

00:09:33.250 --> 00:09:34.030
Zer—

00:09:48.290 --> 00:09:51.180
This doesn't look like one of your traps!

00:09:51.180 --> 00:09:54.100
Mine would have had more style to it.

00:09:54.680 --> 00:09:56.610
Lower your gun.

00:09:56.610 --> 00:09:59.500
I don't know of any Magnums that hold seven rounds—

00:09:59.500 --> 00:10:01.680
There are Walthers with ten shots.

00:10:06.390 --> 00:10:07.320
What?

00:12:02.230 --> 00:12:03.880
Art's nothing special.

00:12:12.840 --> 00:12:14.490
Dead end?

00:12:19.470 --> 00:12:20.490
This again?

00:12:24.560 --> 00:12:25.550
Does this mean something?

00:12:37.340 --> 00:12:39.220
Shall I help you?

00:12:39.220 --> 00:12:41.930
Hmph. So you <i>are</i> still alive.

00:12:41.930 --> 00:12:46.880
You should return what you borrow or people will call you a thief.

00:12:46.880 --> 00:12:50.940
<i>You're</i> the one who stole my bullets and pulled a fast one on me.

00:12:52.790 --> 00:12:57.230
Do you know the safest way to spring a trap?

00:12:57.230 --> 00:13:01.450
You exercise extreme caution and let a skilled gunman handle it.

00:13:01.450 --> 00:13:04.490
But those explosive rounds saved you, didn't they?

00:13:04.490 --> 00:13:07.960
A bullet that explodes upon impact is a wonderful thing.

00:13:08.770 --> 00:13:11.500
Then you should've just switched all six of my bullets.

00:13:11.500 --> 00:13:14.800
Sorry. I only made five.

00:13:14.800 --> 00:13:19.350
That's clever and all, but it looks like you
couldn't manage to open this sarcophagus.

00:13:20.130 --> 00:13:24.670
I bet you were waiting for me to do it because you don't know how.

00:13:25.340 --> 00:13:26.100
This is...

00:13:27.300 --> 00:13:29.390
most likely the release mechanism.

00:13:33.090 --> 00:13:34.900
The weight of sins, huh?

00:13:34.900 --> 00:13:36.110
Pretty interesting.

00:13:36.110 --> 00:13:39.220
The lid will open if we balance it?

00:13:39.220 --> 00:13:41.410
Probably, but it's impossible.

00:13:41.410 --> 00:13:45.810
There's not a person alive who
hasn't sinned. It'll definitely tip.

00:13:45.810 --> 00:13:46.740
Especially—

00:13:46.740 --> 00:13:50.400
Especially for us sinners, right?

00:13:50.400 --> 00:13:51.940
What're you scared of?

00:13:52.520 --> 00:13:58.810
Even without God judging them, everyone knows exactly how much they've sinned, don't they?

00:13:58.810 --> 00:14:01.180
First of all, even if rebirth is the reward,

00:14:01.180 --> 00:14:04.760
there's no guarantee that the next life will be any fun.

00:14:04.760 --> 00:14:08.330
An uncertain future either way, huh.

00:14:08.330 --> 00:14:11.440
That's why it's best to just enjoy it.

00:14:11.440 --> 00:14:15.940
There's nothing wrong with
looking forward to having fun.

00:14:21.510 --> 00:14:22.870
No way!

00:14:26.190 --> 00:14:28.050
Hello there!

00:14:29.750 --> 00:14:31.210
Damn it.

00:14:37.470 --> 00:14:38.680
Future's looking pretty uncertain!

00:14:38.680 --> 00:14:39.940
We'll fall!

00:14:39.940 --> 00:14:41.630
Quick, put the mummy on the pedestal!

00:14:43.190 --> 00:14:44.700
Scorpions!

00:14:44.700 --> 00:14:45.850
They're poisonous!

00:14:48.520 --> 00:14:49.600
Crap!

00:14:49.600 --> 00:14:52.040
There's no way to beat this trap!

00:14:56.030 --> 00:14:57.520
It's a sand whirlpool!

00:14:57.520 --> 00:15:00.780
I don't like rides with too much action!

00:15:01.440 --> 00:15:03.780
How pitiful you look.

00:15:03.780 --> 00:15:05.830
Mine Fujiko!

00:15:05.830 --> 00:15:07.360
You're the girl from before!

00:15:07.360 --> 00:15:09.280
Oh, Mr. Rookie Magnum.

00:15:10.290 --> 00:15:12.290
I remember you.

00:15:12.570 --> 00:15:13.870
Your lower half, that is.

00:15:13.870 --> 00:15:17.150
What? Did you do it with this Magnum guy?

00:15:17.150 --> 00:15:19.020
Don't worry.

00:15:19.020 --> 00:15:22.050
There's nothing "Magnum"
about that part of him at all.

00:15:22.050 --> 00:15:23.900
Right, rookie?

00:15:23.900 --> 00:15:25.140
Don't be ridiculous.

00:15:25.140 --> 00:15:26.940
Who are you calling a rookie?

00:15:27.810 --> 00:15:30.900
So I'm just a pawn that was
sacrificed to trigger the trap?

00:15:30.930 --> 00:15:32.500
Oh, dear.

00:15:32.500 --> 00:15:38.270
I don't mistreat those who try to steal things for me <i>that</i> badly.

00:15:38.270 --> 00:15:41.780
This is the record of another route used by the previous looters.

00:15:41.780 --> 00:15:45.280
The traps on it are mostly broken.

00:15:45.280 --> 00:15:47.280
You sure are a woman who likes secrets.

00:15:47.280 --> 00:15:51.100
Take away a woman's secrets
and she'd have nothing left.

00:15:51.100 --> 00:15:56.290
Also, wouldn't your princess be more
impressed by treasure you risked your life for?

00:15:56.290 --> 00:16:00.460
I've been stuck because I couldn't
figure out how to get past this trap.

00:16:00.460 --> 00:16:01.800
Did you know?

00:16:01.800 --> 00:16:06.180
Falling to the bottom of that
is like being run through a juicer.

00:16:06.180 --> 00:16:07.550
What?

00:16:08.800 --> 00:16:11.710
When the blood of the sacrificed is squeezed out as an offering,

00:16:11.710 --> 00:16:15.810
the peacock gracefully flaps its red wings and soars.

00:16:15.810 --> 00:16:19.630
This juicer is designed to stop when someone falls into it.

00:16:19.630 --> 00:16:23.450
If you want to be saved, why don't you sacrifice Mr. Rookie Magnum here?

00:16:23.450 --> 00:16:24.810
Bye bye.

00:16:25.620 --> 00:16:26.950
Hey, rookie!

00:16:27.700 --> 00:16:29.460
What happened between you and Mine Fujiko?

00:16:29.460 --> 00:16:31.580
You won't be satisfied if I say "nothing", will you?

00:16:31.580 --> 00:16:33.820
How could you just go ahead and...

00:16:33.820 --> 00:16:36.790
You came to a dangerous place
like this for a woman like that?

00:16:36.790 --> 00:16:39.520
It means she's worth that much.

00:16:39.520 --> 00:16:41.550
More than any treasure of gold or silver.

00:16:41.550 --> 00:16:44.550
She's just a woman spreading seeds of trouble.

00:16:45.010 --> 00:16:47.670
I wont steal anything that isn't troublesome.

00:16:47.670 --> 00:16:49.510
That's the Lupin family creed.

00:16:49.510 --> 00:16:51.010
Lupin?

00:16:51.010 --> 00:16:54.360
I see. So you're Lupin III.

00:16:54.360 --> 00:16:56.640
That's good to know.

00:16:56.640 --> 00:16:59.270
Now I can get you a proper tombstone.

00:16:59.270 --> 00:17:01.360
I'd rather you didn't.

00:17:01.360 --> 00:17:03.990
I want to enjoy my life a little longer.

00:17:03.990 --> 00:17:06.230
I suggest you think about your own tombstone.

00:17:06.230 --> 00:17:09.480
Unfortunately, I no longer feel like rushing to my death.

00:17:09.480 --> 00:17:11.410
Maybe because of you.

00:17:26.220 --> 00:17:27.420
It's over.

00:17:29.120 --> 00:17:33.600
Which one will dye the peacock's wings red?

00:17:36.170 --> 00:17:38.320
Wh-What does this mean?

00:17:38.320 --> 00:17:40.940
So scorpion blood is blue, huh?

00:17:40.940 --> 00:17:43.010
Good to know.

00:17:43.010 --> 00:17:43.700
Lupin!

00:17:44.120 --> 00:17:45.450
How—

00:17:50.570 --> 00:17:52.650
Then this blue blood...

00:17:52.650 --> 00:17:55.910
It's from the scorpions that were inside the mummy.

00:17:55.910 --> 00:17:58.290
Sorry, but you guessed wrong.

00:18:01.270 --> 00:18:02.500
What?

00:18:02.500 --> 00:18:04.490
What's going on?

00:18:04.490 --> 00:18:08.770
Could the "blue-winged peacock that brings death" be...

00:18:08.770 --> 00:18:10.610
That's ridiculous!

00:18:14.690 --> 00:18:17.520
The red-winged smiling peacock!

00:18:17.520 --> 00:18:21.020
It's carved from solid alexandrite!

00:18:21.680 --> 00:18:23.130
It's huge.

00:18:23.130 --> 00:18:26.280
The Smithsonian's 60-carat
gem doesn't hold a candle to this.

00:18:27.150 --> 00:18:30.320
How could that have been the "blue peacock that brings death"?

00:18:30.320 --> 00:18:32.740
This is the real smiling peacock!

00:18:32.740 --> 00:18:35.450
The red-winged one that brings wealth—

00:18:44.760 --> 00:18:46.130
Hey!

00:18:46.610 --> 00:18:47.550
Stop it!

00:18:47.550 --> 00:18:49.650
That's <i>my</i> peacock!

00:18:53.840 --> 00:18:54.890
Hey!

00:18:54.890 --> 00:18:56.650
We're gonna get burned to a crisp!

00:19:00.180 --> 00:19:01.850
Traps like these...

00:19:01.850 --> 00:19:05.290
usually have a hidden exit.

00:19:05.290 --> 00:19:09.610
The workers build one so the client can't seal them inside along with the mechanism's secret.

00:19:09.970 --> 00:19:12.840
Hey, there it is.

00:19:24.990 --> 00:19:28.000
It's just an air vent! Not an exit!

00:19:28.000 --> 00:19:31.560
Don't worry. This wall opens up.

00:19:31.560 --> 00:19:33.380
There's a keyhole.

00:19:34.700 --> 00:19:35.760
This shape...

00:19:36.870 --> 00:19:41.770
You've got to be kidding me! I finally got it!

00:19:42.130 --> 00:19:46.020
If bathed in sunlight, alexandrite turns blue.

00:19:46.020 --> 00:19:48.170
Give it up.

00:19:48.170 --> 00:19:52.530
The red peacock that brings wealth exists only inside this pyramid.

00:19:52.530 --> 00:19:58.010
Unless you want to be trapped in here and become the legendary peacock yourself?

00:20:07.320 --> 00:20:10.470
You can take on another challenge, you know.

00:20:10.470 --> 00:20:12.130
You want me, right?

00:20:12.130 --> 00:20:16.130
Something like "steal the 60-carat
one from the Smithsonian"?

00:20:16.130 --> 00:20:21.720
No, the bar rose again. Don't disappoint me!

00:20:22.640 --> 00:20:27.950
Don't you think it would've been better to leave her trapped in there to become the peacock?

00:20:27.950 --> 00:20:29.700
For you and for her.

00:20:29.700 --> 00:20:33.850
Mine Fujiko is a peacock, no matter where she is.

00:20:33.850 --> 00:20:35.780
I don't get your tastes.

00:20:36.700 --> 00:20:39.530
Now, shall we continue where we left off?

00:20:56.070 --> 00:20:58.630
Well, let's save it for another day.

00:20:58.630 --> 00:21:00.450
I'll remember that, rookie.

00:21:00.450 --> 00:21:02.970
It's Jigen. Jigen Daisuke.

00:21:02.970 --> 00:21:05.980
I don't know if I'll be able to remember <i>that</i>.

00:21:13.020 --> 00:21:14.740
A wild one?

00:21:20.710 --> 00:21:26.590
So they really <i>can</i> fly if they feel like it.
